	(text "16C550 UART SUBSYSTEM (LAB 6)\n- U10: 16C550 UART with FIFO (40-pin DIP Socketed)\n- Decoded Base Address: Ports $08-$0F (A0, A1, A2 register select)\n- Pin 40: VDD (+5V), Pin 20: GND\n- C16: 100nF Ceramic Bypass Capacitor mounted directly adjacent to Pin 40\n- Pin 35: MR (Master Reset, active-high RESET_HIGH)\n- Pin 23: /CS2 (nUART_CS from 74HCT138); CS0 and CS1 tied to +5V\n- Pin 21: /RD (nRD), Pin 22: RD (GND); Pin 18: /WR (nWR), Pin 19: WR (GND)\n- Pin 16: XTAL1 (driven by 1.8432 MHz UART_CLK); Pin 17: XTAL2 (Open)\n- Pin 15: RCLK tied directly to Pin 34 (BAUDOUT) for 0% baud rate error (9600-115200 bps)\n- Pin 30: INTR (drives UART_INTR to Sheet 1 inverter U3B)\n- Pin 11: SOUT, Pin 10: SIN, Pin 32: /RTS, Pin 36: /CTS"
		(at 38.1 133.35 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.3 1.3) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000065050090")
	)
	(text "MAX232, DUAL CONNECTORS & CONTENTION ISOLATION (LAB 6)\n- OPERATIONAL MANDATE:\n  *** OPERATOR MUST CONNECT EITHER TTL SERIAL (J4) OR DE-9 RS-232 (J3), BUT NEVER BOTH AT ONCE! ***\n- U11: MAX232 RS-232 Driver/Receiver (DIP-16 Socketed)\n- C17: 100nF Ceramic Bypass Capacitor mounted at Pin 16\n- C18..C21: 0.1uF Ceramic Charge Pump Capacitors (Pins 1-3, 4-5, 2, 6)\n- CONTENTION ISOLATION RESISTORS:\n  - R2 (1k 0.25W): In series between MAX232 R1OUT and 16C550 SIN (RX)\n  - R3 (1k 0.25W): In series between MAX232 R2OUT and 16C550 /CTS\n  - Provides extra safety margin against driver damage if connectors are accidentally cross-connected\n- J3: DE-9 Male Right-Angle Connector (DTE Pinout, Right Edge):\n  - Pin 2: RXD_232, Pin 3: TXD_232, Pin 5: GND, Pin 7: RTS_232, Pin 8: CTS_232\n  - Pins 1, 4, 6, 9: Open (no contention, 5-wire hardware handshaking)\n- J4: 6-Pin 2.54mm Right-Angle TTL Serial Header (Mates directly with DTECH USB-to-TTL FT232RL 6-Pin Cable):\n  - Pin 1: GND (Connects to System Ground) [DTECH Pin 1 Black]\n  - Pin 2: CTS (Connects to 16C550 /RTS Pin 32 -> feeds Cable CTS input) [DTECH Pin 2 Brown]\n  - Pin 3: +5V (Connects to System +5V Rail) [DTECH Pin 3 Red]\n  - Pin 4: TXD (Mates with Cable TXD output -> feeds 16C550 SIN Pin 10) [DTECH Pin 4 Orange]\n  - Pin 5: RXD (Connects to 16C550 SOUT Pin 11 -> feeds Cable RXD input) [DTECH Pin 5 Yellow]\n  - Pin 6: RTS (Mates with Cable RTS output -> feeds 16C550 /CTS Pin 36) [DTECH Pin 6 Green]\n\nHARDWARE INTERRUPT JUMPER:\n- JP4 (JP_INT - 2-pin 2.54mm pitch):\n  - Pin 1: nUART_INT (Active-Low inverted UART interrupt)\n  - Pin 2: nINT (Z80 CPU /INT net, safely pulled high by RN1 when open)\n  - Jumper Open (Default): Polling-only mode (zero interrupt risk)\n  - Jumper Closed: Hardware interrupt service routine mode for advanced labs"
		(at 190.5 133.35 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.3 1.3) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000065050091")
	)
